<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<qti-assessment-item xmlns="http://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/imsqtiasi_v3p0" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/imsqtiasi_v3p0 https://purl.imsglobal.org/spec/qti/v3p0/schema/xsd/imsqti_asiv3p0_v1p0.xsd"
  identifier="sat-c1-u18-deregulation-yourturn" title="Your Turn: Deregulation" adaptive="true" time-dependent="false">

  <qti-response-declaration identifier="RESPONSE" cardinality="single" base-type="identifier">
    <qti-correct-response><qti-value>A</qti-value></qti-correct-response>
  </qti-response-declaration>
  <qti-outcome-declaration identifier="SCORE" cardinality="single" base-type="float">
    <qti-default-value><qti-value>0</qti-value></qti-default-value>
  </qti-outcome-declaration>
  <qti-outcome-declaration identifier="FEEDBACK" cardinality="single" base-type="identifier"/>
  <qti-outcome-declaration identifier="INTERACTION_VISIBILITY" cardinality="single" base-type="identifier">
    <qti-default-value><qti-value>show_interaction</qti-value></qti-default-value>
  </qti-outcome-declaration>

  <qti-item-body>
    <qti-feedback-block identifier="show_interaction" outcome-identifier="INTERACTION_VISIBILITY" show-hide="show" class="qti-margin-0">
      <qti-content-body>
        <qti-choice-interaction response-identifier="RESPONSE" shuffle="true" max-choices="1">
          <qti-prompt>Until last year, anyone selling homemade jams or breads needed a commercial kitchen license, a health permit, and a paid annual inspection. The state then did away with all three requirements for small home producers. Which term best describes the state's change?</qti-prompt>
          <qti-simple-choice identifier="A">deregulation, since it struck the licensing rules off the books for home food sellers</qti-simple-choice>
          <qti-simple-choice identifier="B">accreditation, since it introduced a new official seal that every home producer must now earn</qti-simple-choice>
          <qti-simple-choice identifier="C">a ban, since it outlawed the sale of homemade foods across the state</qti-simple-choice>
          <qti-simple-choice identifier="D">privatization, since it transferred a government-run food service into private hands</qti-simple-choice>
        </qti-choice-interaction>
      </qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>

    <qti-feedback-block identifier="correct" outcome-identifier="FEEDBACK" show-hide="show">
      <qti-content-body><p>Correct. The license, the permit, and the paid inspection all came off the books, leaving home producers free of the state's oversight. Stripping official restrictions away from an activity is deregulation.</p></qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>
    <qti-feedback-block identifier="incorrect" outcome-identifier="FEEDBACK" show-hide="show">
      <qti-content-body><p>Not quite. No new seal was created -- three old requirements disappeared; nothing was outlawed -- selling actually became easier; and the state handed no operation to private owners, because it never ran one. Name the act of taking official rules off an activity.</p></qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>
    <qti-feedback-block identifier="FB-B" outcome-identifier="FEEDBACK" show-hide="show">
      <qti-content-body><p>Inspection would mean Congress began 'examining' airlines' records 'far more closely' — adding oversight. The scenario shows the reverse: rules came off and carriers were left to compete. Name the act of removing restrictions.</p></qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>
    <qti-feedback-block identifier="FB-C" outcome-identifier="FEEDBACK" show-hide="show">
      <qti-content-body><p>Taxation would show up as 'new fees and surcharges' on tickets, but Congress collected nothing — it lifted rules about routes and prices. Adding a financial burden is the opposite of what happened.</p></qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>
    <qti-feedback-block identifier="FB-D" outcome-identifier="FEEDBACK" show-hide="show">
      <qti-content-body><p>Nationalization would place carriers under 'direct public ownership,' the government running them from the capital. Congress moved the opposite direction, loosening its grip so airlines could make their own choices.</p></qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>
  </qti-item-body>

  <qti-response-processing>
    <qti-response-condition>
      <qti-response-if>
        <qti-match><qti-variable identifier="RESPONSE"/><qti-correct identifier="RESPONSE"/></qti-match>
        <qti-set-outcome-value identifier="SCORE"><qti-base-value base-type="float">1</qti-base-value></qti-set-outcome-value>
        <qti-set-outcome-value identifier="completionStatus"><qti-base-value base-type="identifier">completed</qti-base-value></qti-set-outcome-value>
        <qti-set-outcome-value identifier="FEEDBACK"><qti-base-value base-type="identifier">correct</qti-base-value></qti-set-outcome-value>
      </qti-response-if>
      <qti-response-else>
        <qti-set-outcome-value identifier="SCORE"><qti-base-value base-type="float">0</qti-base-value></qti-set-outcome-value>
        <qti-set-outcome-value identifier="completionStatus"><qti-base-value base-type="identifier">incomplete</qti-base-value></qti-set-outcome-value>
        <qti-set-outcome-value identifier="FEEDBACK"><qti-base-value base-type="identifier">incorrect</qti-base-value></qti-set-outcome-value>
      </qti-response-else>
    </qti-response-condition>
    <qti-response-condition>
      <qti-response-if>
        <qti-match><qti-variable identifier="RESPONSE"/><qti-base-value base-type="identifier">B</qti-base-value></qti-match>
        <qti-set-outcome-value identifier="FEEDBACK"><qti-base-value base-type="identifier">FB-B</qti-base-value></qti-set-outcome-value>
      </qti-response-if>
    </qti-response-condition>
    <qti-response-condition>
      <qti-response-if>
        <qti-match><qti-variable identifier="RESPONSE"/><qti-base-value base-type="identifier">C</qti-base-value></qti-match>
        <qti-set-outcome-value identifier="FEEDBACK"><qti-base-value base-type="identifier">FB-C</qti-base-value></qti-set-outcome-value>
      </qti-response-if>
    </qti-response-condition>
    <qti-response-condition>
      <qti-response-if>
        <qti-match><qti-variable identifier="RESPONSE"/><qti-base-value base-type="identifier">D</qti-base-value></qti-match>
        <qti-set-outcome-value identifier="FEEDBACK"><qti-base-value base-type="identifier">FB-D</qti-base-value></qti-set-outcome-value>
      </qti-response-if>
    </qti-response-condition>
  </qti-response-processing>
</qti-assessment-item>
